# Visual verification

## Visual QA loop (every UI change and every UI phase gate)
`/visual-qa` captures every screen state at desktop 1440, tablet 834 and mobile 412 px in the light theme (dark theme deferred: re-enable with `--themes light,dark` or `BF_VISUAL_THEMES=light,dark`), collects console errors, failed requests, horizontal overflow, unrendered interpolation and layout shift, compares with the approved Stitch design, and the agent opens every screenshot, fixes issues and re-runs until no blocking findings remain (at most 5 iterations). Never report a screen done with blocking findings. Then the `ux-reviewer` subagent reviews the evidence independently.

## Design parity
- Approved Stitch exports live in `design/stitch/<NNN-slug>/<state>--<viewport>--<theme>.png` (screen number first; `design/stitch/README.md`). Export with the Stitch MCP (`get_screen` for `screenshot.name`, then `download_file`) and save with `scripts/visual/stitch-save.mjs`.
- `scripts/visual/design-parity.mjs` writes side-by-side and diff images. The mismatch ratio is advisory; the agent's inspection decides, judged against the design and the budget-safety visual rules in `frontend-angular.mdc`.

## Visual regression baselines
- `apps/web-e2e/src/visual/visual.spec.ts` takes `toHaveScreenshot` baselines for every entry in `apps/web-e2e/visual/screens.json` (the same file the QA loop reads), per viewport, in the `visual-light` project (dark theme deferred: add a `visual-dark` project with `colorScheme: 'dark'` when it is re-enabled).
- Determinism: deterministic seed, frozen clock (`freezeTime`), fonts loaded (`document.fonts.ready`), animations and caret disabled, reduced motion, `scale: 'css'`, dynamic regions (relative times, ids, live counters) masked. Thresholds: `maxDiffPixelRatio` 0.002, `threshold` 0.2; raise only per screen with a reason.
- Baselines are created and compared only in the pinned image `mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.64.1-noble` through `scripts/visual/pw-docker.sh`, locally and in CI, so renders match. The Playwright version in `package.json`, `pw-docker.sh`, `setup-tools.sh` and CI must agree (harness validation checks it).
- Intentional updates only via `npm run e2e:update-snapshots`, with "Visual baselines updated: <reason>" in the PR description (CI fails otherwise). Never edit or delete baseline PNGs by hand to make a run pass.

## Artifacts
Diffs, the Playwright HTML report and visual QA reports are CI artifacts; traces, videos and saved auth state contain tokens and stay in `dist/.playwright/` and `tmp/`, never in git.
